+# The Daily Grind
+
+Run `pnpm start` to serve the site and `npm test` to run the automated timing tests.
+
+## Contentful update timing
+
+`performance.js` automatically observes browser-attributed interaction contentful
+paints and client-side soft navigations. All durations are in milliseconds:
+
+- Interaction records report `duration` from the initiating input to presentation
+  of the new content. Successively larger paints produce additional records.
+- Soft navigation records report `fcpDuration` and `lcpDuration` from the
+  initiating input. LCP is finalized on the next soft navigation, when the page
+  is hidden, on `pagehide`, or when explicitly flushed. A missing candidate is
+  reported as `null`.
+
+Inspect `window.dailyGrindPerformance.supported` for browser capabilities and
+`window.dailyGrindPerformance.getMeasurements()` for the latest 200 records.
+Consume records as they arrive with:
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => {
+  console.log(detail);
+});
+```
+
+`window.dailyGrindPerformance.flush()` drains pending observer entries and
+finalizes the active route. `stop()` also disconnects observers and removes
+lifecycle listeners. Measurements stay in memory; no analytics endpoint is
+configured and no network requests are made by the instrumentation.
+
+These APIs are progressive enhancements: unsupported entry types are skipped.
+INP, initial-load LCP, and frame callbacks are not substituted for contentful
+update timing. The current site's links perform document navigations; soft
+navigation records apply if browser-detected client-side routing is introduced.
